  "final_answer_preview": "The distinction between hurt and grievous hurt is outlined in the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. Hurt is a general term for any bodily injury, whereas grievous hurt is defined in Section 116 as a type of hurt that includes specific severe injuries such as emasculation, permanent loss of sight or hearing, and any hurt that endangers life or causes severe bodily pain for at least fifteen days. Additionally, Section 117 specifies that a person is said to voluntarily cause grievous hurt if they intend to cause grievous hurt and actually do so.",
